# Arr API Pattern

When writing Tdarr plugins that interact with Sonarr/Radarr:

## Headers & Host

```typescript
const headers = {
  'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  'X-Api-Key': String(args.inputs.arr_api_key),
  Accept: 'application/json',
};
const arrHost = String(args.inputs.arr_host).trim().replace(/\/$/, '');
```

## ID Lookup (two-step)

1. Try IMDB regex on file path: `/\b(tt|nm|co|ev|ch|ni)\d{7,10}?\b/i`
2. If found: `GET /api/v3/{movie|series}/lookup?term=imdb:{id}`
3. Fallback: `GET /api/v3/parse?title={encodedFilename}` — response shape differs:
   - Radarr: `data.movie.id`, `data.parsedMovieInfo.releaseGroup`
   - Sonarr: `data.series.id`, `data.parsedEpisodeInfo.releaseGroup`

## Delegate Pattern

Use `arr` dropdown input (`radarr` | `sonarr`) to switch endpoint names (`movie` vs `series`) and response accessors.

## Refresh After Update

```typescript
POST /api/v3/command
// Radarr: { name: "RefreshMovie", movieIds: [id] }
// Sonarr: { name: "RefreshSeries", seriesId: id }
```

## Parse Endpoint

Stateless — just parses a filename string. File doesn't need to exist in arr. Useful for extracting release group without needing a media ID.
